Chapter: RocRecLogicMatch
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_recursive_data_tests.zig,
 "recursive nominal logic nested match":

     Logic := [True, False, And(Logic, Logic), Or(Logic, Logic), Not(Logic)]
     main = match Logic.And(Logic.Or(Logic.True, Logic.False), Logic.Not(Logic.False)) {
         And(Or(True, False), Not(False)) => "ok"
         _ => "bad"
     }

 A pattern three constructors deep. `True` and `False` are Codex's Boolean
 literals, so the constructors are `LTrue` and `LFalse`. A second line
 evaluates the formula, which is the value the pattern is asserting the
 shape of.

Section: Types

  Logic =
   | LTrue
   | LFalse
   | And (Logic) (Logic)
   | Or (Logic) (Logic)
   | Not (Logic)

Section: Functions

  shape-check : Logic -> Text
  shape-check (v) =
   when v
    is And (Or (LTrue) (LFalse)) (Not (LFalse)) -> "ok"
    is otherwise -> "bad"

  logic-eval : Logic -> Boolean
  logic-eval (v) =
   when v
    is LTrue -> True
    is LFalse -> False
    is And (a) (b) -> if logic-eval a then logic-eval b else False
    is Or (a) (b) -> if logic-eval a then True else logic-eval b
    is Not (a) -> if logic-eval a then False else True

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let formula = And (Or LTrue LFalse) (Not LFalse)
   in act
    print-line-uni (shape-check formula)
    print-line-uni (if logic-eval formula then "true" else "false")
   end
  end
